WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.230
You can spot an AI deck in a second: gradients, identical cards,

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.810
and very happy stock-photo people.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.450
That's because Claude doesn't know your taste yet, so you get the average.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.410
It's like the hairdresser: ask for something nice, get their usual cut.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.950
Bring a picture, get yours.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:28.190
Still, the brand is covered, so you add your taste in two layers, both from a mood board: a visual language for everything,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.370
and a look for each piece, refreshed whenever you change your mind.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:37.710
So in this adventure, you learn Claude Design with Monday's design system,

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:42.050
bringing your own taste and what each piece needs to every deck or design.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:46.070
Then you build a new-look skill on top of any skills you use,

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:51.510
pick from a few directions, and direct in rounds until you'd show it with your name on it.
